[0.046, "o", "go build -ldflags \"-X main.version=d0f1af4-dirty\" -o bin/portalguard ./cmd/portalguard\r\n"]
[0.299, "o", "this needs root and CUTS THE NETWORK several times on purpose.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "sudo ./testenv/demo.sh\r\n"]
[0.022, "o", "Password:"]
[5.543, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.519, "o", "portalguard: IDLE --DETECT--> DETECTING\r\n"]
[0.045, "o", "portalguard: DETECTING --PORTAL_FOUND--> PORTAL_FOUND (127.0.0.1)\r\n"]
[0.024, "o", "portalguard: PORTAL_FOUND --LOCKDOWN--> LOCKED_DOWN (pf)\r\n"]
[0.033, "o", "portalguard: gap opened for 127.0.0.1 [127.0.0.1] ports=[80 443 8080] dns=false\r\n"]
[0.028, "o", "portalguard: gap opened for network resolvers [192.168.0.1 fd12:3456:789a::53] ports=[53] dns=true\r\nportalguard: LOCKED_DOWN --OPEN_GAP--> GAP_OPEN (127.0.0.1)\r\n\r\nOpen this page and log in yourself:\r\n  http://127.0.0.1:8080/login\r\n\r\nEverything else on this machine is blocked while you do.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "Waiting up to 1m0s for the login to go through...\r\n"]
[8.033, "o", "portalguard: GAP_OPEN --AUTHENTICATED--> AUTHENTICATED (re-probe reached the real internet)\r\n"]
[0.067, "o", "portalguard: AUTHENTICATED --SEAL--> SEALED (gap closed)\r\n\r\nAuthenticated and sealed. Traffic is still blocked.\r\n\r\n--- what happened while portalguard was engaged ---\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "The gap was open for 8s.\r\nHeld back 298 packets (198.4 kB) your machine tried to send while locked down.\r\nDropped 34 packets (5.8 kB) the network tried to send you.\r\n\r\n20 packets (2.4 kB) went out through the DNS hole, to 192.168.0.1, fd12:3456:789a::53.\r\nThat is packets, not lookups: a query and its reply are counted separately.\r\nHostnames queried: other (5 hostnames)\r\nThe kernel did not attribute these queries to a process.\r\n\r\nSource: pf rule counters, pfctl -a portalguard -s rules -v\r\n---\r\nBring up your VPN now, then run: sudo ./bin/portalguard release\r\n"]
